    "text": "The figure represents a voltage regulator circuit using a Zener diode. The breakdown voltage of the Zener diode is <math><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and the load resistance is, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . The series resistance of the circuit is <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . If the battery voltage <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> varies from <math><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> , what are the minimum and maximum values of the current through Zener diode?<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/02d4a28e-c453-4769-9701-db0d02a487bb-image.png\" style=\"width: 314px; height: 204px;\" />",
